parameters.help_en:
The script of the Data Integration synchronization task.
The following types of synchronization tasks can be created: 
Synchronize data from MySQL to MaxCompute.
Synchronize data from MySQL to Kafka.
Synchronize data from MySQL to Hologres.

SelectedTables is used to select synchronization tables in multi-database mode, and Tables is used to select synchronization tables in single-database mode.
If the script contains the SelectedTables statement, the system uses the table information in the SelectedTables statement for synchronization.
If the script contains the Tables statement, the system uses the field information of Tables for synchronization.


The following example shows the script for synchronizing data from MySQL to MaxCompute:
```
{
  "type": "realtime",
  "version": "1.0",
  "setting": {
    "resourceGroup": "S_res_group_280749521950784_1623033752022",
    "taskType": "oneclick_to_odps"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "stepType": "mysql",
      "parameter": {
        "connection": [
          {
            "datasourceType": "mysql",
            "datasource": "mysql_pub1",
            "selectedTables": [
              {
                "dbName": "mysql_db",
                "schema": [
                  {
                    "tableInfos": [
                      {
                        "table": "molin_di_test_in_pk_v4"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "Reader",
      "category": "reader"
    },
    {
      "stepType": "odps",
      "parameter": {
        "datasource": "odps_source"
      },
      "name": "Writer",
      "category": "writer"
    }
  ]
}
```

